IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Age of Majority Act 1972 (Western Australia) -- when a person attains an age (s 4), when a person attains full age
-- and full capacity at 18 (s 5(1)), how "full age", "adult", "infant", "minor" and like words in other laws are read
-- (s 5(2), (3), (5), (7)), and that incapacities not due to age remain (s 5(4)).
--
-- SEAT: the young person turning 18. Every decision is phrased as that person would ask it: "When do I reach this
-- age", "When do I come of full age", "Am I an adult in law on this day", "Does this word in that law mean 18 for me",
-- "Does turning 18 remove this incapacity".
--
-- Provisions covered: s 3 (enactment, instrument, laws of the State, commencing day), s 4(1), (2), s 5(1)(a), (b),
-- s 5(2)(a), (b), s 5(3), s 5(4), s 5(5), s 5(7)(a)-(c).
--
-- Edition: the reprint compiled as at 22 August 2003 (amendments to No. 14 of 1996), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/act-1972-46.txt (retrieved 7 September 2026). No regulations: the Act has none to set
-- its numbers. The COMMENCING DAY (the day fixed by proclamation under s 2) is not in the deposit -- the compilation
-- table and the proclamation are omitted -- so it is an input to every question that needs it.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 5(6) (orders before the commencing day about money recovered for a minor), s 5(8) (property absolutely
-- vested before the commencing day), s 5(9) (an enactment incorporated in an instrument the Act does not affect),
-- s 5(10), (11) (limitation periods for causes of action arising before the commencing day): all transitional, and
-- none can reach a person born after the commencing day. Machinery out: ss 1, 2; the amendments of other Acts and the
-- Schedule, omitted from the reprint under the Reprints Act 1984. What follows from full age under OTHER laws (voting,
-- marriage, wills, liquor, juries, powers of attorney) is for those Acts' own encodings; this Act only fixes the line.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Age of Majority Act 1972 -- the young person's questions`

§§ `s 4 -- the moment I reach an age`

-- s 4(1): "For all the purposes of the laws of the State, the time at which a person attains a particular age expressed
-- in years shall be the commencement of the relevant anniversary of the date of his birth."
-- s 4(2): "This section has effect only where the relevant anniversary falls on the commencing day or on a subsequent
-- day."
-- The Act does not say which day is the "anniversary" of 29 February in a year with no 29 February. The encoding does
-- not guess (1 March or 28 February): it says the Act does not fix it.
DECLARE `When I reach the age` IS ONE OF
    `at the very start of`
        HAS `the day` IS A DATE                -- "the commencement of the relevant anniversary": the first moment of that day
    `not fixed by s 4: the anniversary fell before the commencing day`
    `not fixed by the Act: I was born on 29 February and that year has no 29 February`

-- The anniversary built from the birth date by adding to the YEAR (leap-safe). The lenient Date constructor rolls
-- 29 February of a common year to 1 March; that roll is detected, not used.
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE, `the age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the anniversary` MEANS
    Date (DATE_DAY `my date of birth`) (DATE_MONTH `my date of birth`) (DATE_YEAR `my date of birth` PLUS `the age`)

GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE, `the age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the anniversary does not exist` IF
        DATE_MONTH `my date of birth` EQUALS 2
    AND DATE_DAY `my date of birth` EQUALS 29
    AND (NOT (DATE_MONTH (`the anniversary` `my date of birth` `the age`) EQUALS 2))

@export When, in law, do I reach a given age (Age of Majority Act 1972 (WA) s 4)?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth, ISO 8601
      `the age` IS A NUMBER @desc The age in years you are asking about, for example 18
      `the commencing day` IS A DATE @desc The day the Age of Majority Act 1972 came into operation, fixed by proclamation under s 2 (not in the deposited text), ISO 8601
GIVETH A `When I reach the age`
DECIDE `When do I reach this age` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the anniversary does not exist` `my date of birth` `the age`
            THEN `not fixed by the Act: I was born on 29 February and that year has no 29 February`
        IF `the anniversary` `my date of birth` `the age` LESS THAN `the commencing day`
            THEN `not fixed by s 4: the anniversary fell before the commencing day`
        OTHERWISE `at the very start of` (`the anniversary` `my date of birth` `the age`)

§§ `s 5(1) -- when I come of full age and full capacity`

-- s 5(1): "for all the purposes of the laws of the State -- (a) a person who, on or after the commencing day, attains the
-- age of 18 years attains full age and full capacity on attaining that age; and (b) a person who, on the commencing day,
-- is of or over the age of 18 years but under the age of 21 years attains full age and full capacity on that day."
-- A person 21 or over on the commencing day is in neither limb: the Act does not say when that person came of full age
-- (the encoder infers it was under the earlier law, which the deposit does not state). Whether a person was 18 or 21
-- "on the commencing day" is reckoned here by the anniversary, as in s 4; for an anniversary before the commencing day
-- s 4 does not apply (s 4(2)) and the Act does not say how it is reckoned -- the encoder's reading.
DECLARE `When I come of full age` IS ONE OF
    `on attaining 18, at the very start of`              -- s 5(1)(a)
        HAS `the day` IS A DATE
    `on the commencing day`                               -- s 5(1)(b)
        HAS `the day` IS A DATE
    `not decided by this Act: I was 21 or over on the commencing day`
    `not decided by this Act: I was born on 29 February and my 18th year has no 29 February`

-- "full age": the age of 18 years, s 5(1).
`the age of full age` MEANS 18
-- the upper bound in s 5(1)(b).
`the old age of majority` MEANS 21

@export When do I come of full age and full capacity (Age of Majority Act 1972 (WA) s 5(1))?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth, ISO 8601
      `the commencing day` IS A DATE @desc The day the Age of Majority Act 1972 came into operation, fixed by proclamation under s 2 (not in the deposited text), ISO 8601
GIVETH A `When I come of full age`
DECIDE `When do I come of full age` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the anniversary does not exist` `my date of birth` `the age of full age`
            THEN `not decided by this Act: I was born on 29 February and my 18th year has no 29 February`
        IF `the anniversary` `my date of birth` `the age of full age` AT LEAST `the commencing day`
            THEN `on attaining 18, at the very start of` (`the anniversary` `my date of birth` `the age of full age`)
        IF `the anniversary` `my date of birth` `the old age of majority` GREATER THAN `the commencing day`
            THEN `on the commencing day` `the commencing day`
        OTHERWISE `not decided by this Act: I was 21 or over on the commencing day`

DECLARE `Am I an adult in law` IS ONE OF
    `yes: of full age and full capacity under s 5(1)(a)`
    `yes: of full age and full capacity under s 5(1)(b)`
    `not yet: I am not of full age on that day`
    `not decided by this Act: I was 21 or over on the commencing day`
    `not decided by this Act: I was born on 29 February and my 18th year has no 29 February`

@export Am I an adult in law (of full age and full capacity) on a given day (Age of Majority Act 1972 (WA) s 5(1))?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth, ISO 8601
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about, ISO 8601
      `the commencing day` IS A DATE @desc The day the Age of Majority Act 1972 came into operation, fixed by proclamation under s 2 (not in the deposited text), ISO 8601
GIVETH A `Am I an adult in law`
DECIDE `Am I an adult in law on this day` IS
    CONSIDER `When do I come of full age` `my date of birth` `the commencing day`
    WHEN `on attaining 18, at the very start of` d THEN
        IF `the day asked about` AT LEAST d
            THEN `yes: of full age and full capacity under s 5(1)(a)`
            ELSE `not yet: I am not of full age on that day`
    WHEN `on the commencing day` d THEN
        IF `the day asked about` AT LEAST d
            THEN `yes: of full age and full capacity under s 5(1)(b)`
            ELSE `not yet: I am not of full age on that day`
    WHEN `not decided by this Act: I was 21 or over on the commencing day`
        THEN `not decided by this Act: I was 21 or over on the commencing day`
    WHEN `not decided by this Act: I was born on 29 February and my 18th year has no 29 February`
        THEN `not decided by this Act: I was born on 29 February and my 18th year has no 29 February`

§§ `s 5(2), (3), (5), (7) -- what "full age", "adult", "infant" or "minor" means in another law`

-- s 5(2): s 5(1) "applies and has effect, in the absence of a definition or of an indication of a contrary intention,
-- for the purposes of the construction of the expressions 'majority', 'full age', 'adult', 'full capacity', 'sui juris',
-- and similar expressions, and the expressions 'infant', 'infancy', 'minor', 'nonage', 'minority', and similar
-- expressions in -- (a) an enactment, whether passed or made before, on, or after the commencing day; and (b) an
-- instrument executed or made on or after that day."
-- s 5(3): "This section does not apply so as to affect the operation or construction of any reference in an enactment
-- or instrument to an age expressed in years."
DECLARE `The expression` IS ONE OF
    `majority`
    `full age`
    `adult`
    `full capacity`
    `sui juris`                       -- "of one's own right": legally able to act for oneself
    `infant`
    `infancy`
    `minor`
    `nonage`                          -- the state of being under age
    `minority`
    `a similar expression`            -- s 5(2) "and similar expressions"; whether a word is similar is asked as a fact
    `an age expressed in years`       -- for example "21 years of age" (s 5(3))

-- s 3: "enactment" -- an Act or provision, an Imperial Act applying in the State, and regulations, rules, local laws,
-- by-laws, orders in Council, proclamations, notices and the like made under them. "instrument" -- "any written document
-- of whatsoever nature", not an enactment and not a law of the Commonwealth or of another State or a document under such
-- a law. "laws of the State" does not include a law of the Commonwealth.
-- s 5(5): a will or codicil executed before the commencing day is not treated as made on or after it "by reason only that
-- the will or codicil is confirmed by a codicil executed on or after that day".
-- s 5(7): s 5 does not affect "(a) any industrial award, order, determination or agreement; (b) any instrument made or
-- entered into pursuant to any enactment prescribing wages and other conditions of or relating to apprenticeship;
-- (c) any provisions of any enactment governing or relating to conditions of employment or rights or obligations arising
-- from employment."
DECLARE `Where the expression appears` IS ONE OF
    `a WA enactment`                                                           -- whenever passed or made
    `a written instrument made on or after the commencing day`                 -- a contract, a will, a trust deed, ...
    `a written instrument made before the commencing day`
    `a will made before the commencing day, confirmed by a codicil on or after it`
    `a Commonwealth law, another State's law, or a document under one`
    `an industrial award, order, determination or agreement`
    `an apprenticeship instrument made under an enactment on wages and conditions`
    `a provision of an enactment on conditions of employment`

DECLARE `How the expression is read` IS ONE OF
    `with 18 as the line: full age and full capacity as in s 5(1)`
    `as that law defines it or as its contrary intention shows`
    `not affected: the age in years stands as written (s 5(3))`
    `not affected: an instrument made before the commencing day (s 5(2)(b))`
    `not affected: a will made before the commencing day is not remade by a later codicil (s 5(2)(b), (5))`
    `not affected: this Act reaches only the laws of the State (ss 3, 5(1))`
    `not affected: employment and industrial instruments are excluded (s 5(7))`

GIVEN `the place` IS A `Where the expression appears`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is excluded by s 5(7)` IF
    CONSIDER `the place`
    WHEN `an industrial award, order, determination or agreement` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an apprenticeship instrument made under an enactment on wages and conditions` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a provision of an enactment on conditions of employment` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

@export Does a word like "full age", "adult", "infant" or "minor" in another law mean 18 for me (Age of Majority Act 1972 (WA) s 5(2))?
GIVEN `the expression` IS A `The expression` @desc The word or phrase used in the other law or document
      `the place` IS A `Where the expression appears` @desc The kind of law or document it appears in
      `it has its own definition or a contrary intention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that law or document defines the word itself, or shows it means something else
GIVETH A `How the expression is read`
DECIDE `How is this expression read` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the expression` EQUALS `an age expressed in years`
            THEN `not affected: the age in years stands as written (s 5(3))`
        IF `the place` EQUALS `a Commonwealth law, another State's law, or a document under one`
            THEN `not affected: this Act reaches only the laws of the State (ss 3, 5(1))`
        IF `is excluded by s 5(7)` `the place`
            THEN `not affected: employment and industrial instruments are excluded (s 5(7))`
        IF `the place` EQUALS `a written instrument made before the commencing day`
            THEN `not affected: an instrument made before the commencing day (s 5(2)(b))`
        IF `the place` EQUALS `a will made before the commencing day, confirmed by a codicil on or after it`
            THEN `not affected: a will made before the commencing day is not remade by a later codicil (s 5(2)(b), (5))`
        IF `it has its own definition or a contrary intention`
            THEN `as that law defines it or as its contrary intention shows`
        OTHERWISE `with 18 as the line: full age and full capacity as in s 5(1)`

§§ `s 5(4) -- what turning 18 does not cure`

-- s 5(4): "This section does not affect any deficiency of juristic competence or capacity that is attributable to
-- insanity, or mental infirmity, or any other factor distinct from age."
DECLARE `The cause of the incapacity` IS ONE OF
    `my age`
    `insanity`
    `mental infirmity`
    `another factor distinct from age`        -- for example a court order or a bankruptcy (the encoder's examples)

@export Does attaining full age at 18 remove this incapacity (Age of Majority Act 1972 (WA) s 5(4))?
GIVEN `the cause` IS A `The cause of the incapacity` @desc What the lack of legal capacity is due to
      `I have attained full age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have come of full age under s 5(1)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does turning 18 remove this incapacity` IF
        `I have attained full age`
    AND `the cause` EQUALS `my age`
